# Rust REST implementation scaffolds for `{{ .SchemaName }}`

Starter implementations of the generated `{{ .CrateName }}` server's
namespace traits. Mount this directory as a module of the service's crate,
which depends on `{{ .CrateName }}`, `{{ .RuntimeCrate }}` and
`async-trait`:

```rust
#[path = "<this directory>/mod.rs"]
mod implementations;
```

- `mod.rs` declares one module per namespace.
- In each namespace directory, `implementation.rs` holds the
  `Implementation` struct and its one impl of the namespace trait, which
  hands each method to the function of the same name in its own file. A
  method takes the operation's `<Operation>Args`, its arguments decoded
  and checked by the router, and returns the operation's result type.
- An operation declared `@manualRouteRegistration` has no file: the
  service mounts its route itself (see `build_router`).
- Existing files are never overwritten. An operation added to the schema
  later needs its method in `implementation.rs`, a line in `mod.rs` and a
  file of its own, which the compiler points at.

Regenerate safely:

```bash
superschematic build schemas/services/{{ .SchemaName }}
```
